Forget about using dos to compile. It's not designed for it and it's
clumsy as hell. Get djgpp with bash and follow the installation text
files. Along with the installation instructions in the top level readme in
the nethack source code. *After* it's patched. *Follow* the instructions.
They're there for a reason. You will need bash, gcc, libc, yacc (or
byacc), the binutils and termcap and ncurses. Everything else - like the
ide is gravy. This gives you the *text* version of nethack. The problems
creating the gui version simply aren't worth it for the trouble of
compiling in M$ land. 

http://www.delorie.com/djgpp/

Patching is something you do to source code before it's compiled.
Therefore you *have* to know how to do both to do it at all. There is no
easy way to do it otherwise. 


